From d61e5771db271d857acfa4b39fd929d49d4b4d93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qiyinxi <qiyinxi@foxmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 20:50:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 52/57] media: return textures of frames dropped while loading
 a snapshot

When a snapshot is loaded, the H.264, HEVC and VP8/VP9 decoders replay
the packets saved since the last key frame through oneShotDecode(),
which receives the decoded frames and drops them. load() only tells
the video helper to ignore its output when mVideoHelper is set. With
the CUDA decoder the helper is still mHwVideoHelper at that point (the
VP8/VP9 decoder moves it to mVideoHelper only in the first
try_decode()), so in GPU texture mode every replayed frame takes a
Y/UV texture pair from the pool, and dropping the frame leaks the pair
until the GL share group goes away: about 3 MB per frame at 1080p.

Hand the pairs of the dropped frames back to the pool. Frames decoded
into a byte buffer carry no texture names and are dropped as before.
Returning the pairs works whichever helper produced the frames and
however the decoders shuffle them, so it is used rather than switching
the hardware helper to ignore its output during the replay.

The VP8/VP9 oneShotDecode() decodes every packet twice, through
decode_internal() and again through mVideoHelper->decode(), so it
leaked two pairs per replayed packet. This change leaves the double
decode alone.

Test: snapshots saved while a guest decoded 1080p video with the CUDA
      decoder in GPU texture mode, then loaded, with a debugger
      counting. Without this change the VP9 decoder replayed 38
      packets, uploaded 76 frames into textures and returned none of
      the pairs; with it, 37 packets, 74 frames, 74 pairs returned.
      H.264 replays with it: 2 and 3 frames, all returned.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:Claude-Opus-5.5
Change-Id: I9067b7b50f6260a2210d621c5873d3dd64628a5d
---
 .../src/android/emulation/MediaH264DecoderGeneric.cpp      | 7 +++++++
 .../src/android/emulation/MediaHevcDecoderGeneric.cpp      | 7 +++++++
 .../media/src/android/emulation/MediaVpxDecoderGeneric.cpp | 7 +++++++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/android/emu/media/src/android/emulation/MediaH264DecoderGeneric.cpp b/android/emu/media/src/android/emulation/MediaH264DecoderGeneric.cpp
index 9c4398078..8507b727f 100644
--- a/android/emu/media/src/android/emulation/MediaH264DecoderGeneric.cpp
+++ b/android/emu/media/src/android/emulation/MediaH264DecoderGeneric.cpp
@@ -481,6 +481,13 @@ void MediaH264DecoderGeneric::oneShotDecode(const uint8_t* data,
         if (!success) {
             break;
         }
+        // The frame is dropped. If it was decoded to GPU textures, its pair
+        // came from the pool; hand it back, or the textures leak.
+        if (frame.texture.size() >= 2 && frame.texture[0] > 0 &&
+            frame.texture[1] > 0) {
+            mRenderer.putTextureFrame(
+                    TextureFrame{frame.texture[0], frame.texture[1]});
+        }
     }
 }
 
